    "title": "Two John Deere zero-turn mowers stolen in Daviess County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Andrew Newland ,\n1 hours ago\nDAVIESS COUNTY, Ind. (WEHT) — The Daviess County Sheriff’s Office is searching for a suspect they say stole two lawn mowers.\nDeputies say two John Deere zero-turn mowers were stolen from the 3200 block of Carter Road sometime over the weekend. Both mowers were last observed traveling onto Buckland Square Drive.\nThose that have information that may identify the suspect pictured above are asked to contact Detective Nathan Godeke at (270) 685-8444.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "(WEHT) — The Daviess County Sheriff’s Office is searching for a suspect they say stole two lawn mowers. Deputies say two John Deere zero-turn mowers were stolen from the 3200 block of Carter Road sometime over the weekend. Both mowers were last observed traveling onto Buckland Square Drive. Those that have information that may identify the suspect pictured above are asked to contact Detective Nathan Godeke at (270) 685-8444. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
